<title>JAPAN: Yen reflects G7 accord on stable rates - Sakakibara.</title>
<headline>Yen reflects G7 accord on stable rates - Sakakibara.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monday afternoon's rate of around 122.50 yen to the dollar reflects a Group of Seven (G7) agreement on the need for currency market stability, Eisuke Sakakibara, director-general of the Japanese Finance Ministry's International Finance Bureau, told a parliamentary committee  </p>
<p>&quot;We have been seeking a stable foreign exchange market and have said that excessive fluctuations were undesirable, which was stated in the G7 statement. The currency rate today reflects that and is at 122.50 yen (to the dollar),&quot; Sakakibara said.</p>
</text>
